   793                              <1> ; sd_cmd -- send command AL with argument EBX and CRC byte AH (end bit
   794                              <1> ; included; only CMD0 and CMD8 are checked in SPI mode), and return its
   795                              <1> ; R1 in AL.  AL = FFh and CF set if no answer started in the window.  The
   796                              <1> ; card must be selected.  Leaves the transaction positioned after R1, at
   797                              <1> ; the offset found, for rd_abyte and rd_ablock.
   798                              <1> ;
   799                              <1> ; One burst of WINLEN bytes: FF, 40|cmd, the argument big end first, the
   800                              <1> ; CRC, FF, then sixteen more FFs to clock the answer in.  R1's bit 7 is
   801                              <1> ; always 0 and the card sends FFs until it answers, so the first 0 bit
   802                              <1> ; from byte 6 on (an answer can start in byte 7, and arrive a bit early)
   803                              <1> ; is the top bit of R1.
